meet rody Smith a 25 year old internet  superstar from Florida since he started  high school he's become an undisputed  master of the frisbee no target is too  small or too far away for Brody I've  been playing frisbee for about 7 years  now so I would have to probably say over  my lifetime I've probably found easily  close to a million times but in 2011  Brody pulled off this most epic throw to  date with this monster 500 foot effort  off the Narrows Bridge in Perth  Australia this never before performed  throw earns Brody the 15th spot on our  countdown where its mixture of skill  coordination and execution I had a  little little patriotic tear when I  realized all this was going down in  Perth Western Australia now I've  actually been on that bridge it's windy  up there and not only that but it's a  long way up the wind was coming off my  back right shoulder and as far as the  frisbee is concerned when you throw it  it always wants to try to be level so I  wanted to make sure that I put the edge  on it like this to where the wind was  gonna push it to make it level what's  happening is this frisbees moving to you  and the arrow is traveling a further  distance on the top than is on the  bottom which is creating a low-pressure  zone up here and that's causing lift on  this frisbee so that's what's keeping it  going up as it's going along but  normally the frisbee if we were just  pushed through the air would start  tumbling but that's where the spinning  comes in if something spinning it  doesn't like to be tilted it doesn't  like to change its momentum so the  moment you try and tilt it it resists  that tilt you can't spin a frisbee too  fast faster it's going the more stable  it will be and it will hold this  perfectly level pattern for pretty much  as far as it can keep going while  spinning so while we enjoy Brody's epic  throw one last time watch this space  because we have a feeling this won't be  the last time the internet sees a clip  of Brody's fantastic 